course: dictionary
lesson: 11957
title: Cartilaginous: bendy, not bony
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words describe what something is made of. Cartilaginous is one of them. Look at the word in parts: cartilage, the tough, bendy tissue, plus the ending -ous, which often means full of or having. So cartilaginous means made of cartilage. «Feel the top of your ear, it is soft and bendy, not hard like a bone.» Your ear is partly cartilaginous.
explain: Context shows you the difference. «The shark has a cartilaginous skeleton, so its body is light and flexible.» The word tells you the skeleton is bendy. «The goldfish has a bony skeleton.» Bony means made of hard bone. The two sentences show two different kinds of skeleton.
explain: Scientists sort fish into groups by their skeletons. «Sharks, rays and skates are cartilaginous fish.» «Salmon and goldfish are bony fish.» To check a new word, swap in your meaning: "Sharks, rays and skates are made of cartilage." It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Cartilage is a tough, bendy tissue, not as hard as bone.
fact: «Cartilaginous» means made of cartilage.
fact: Cartilage is found in your ears, your nose and the ends of your bones, where it cushions your joints.
fact: Sharks, rays and skates are cartilaginous fish, with skeletons made of cartilage instead of bone.
fact: Goldfish and salmon are bony fish, with skeletons made of bone.
exercise: «Sharks and rays have cartilaginous skeletons.» What does cartilaginous mean here? | Very fast | Very cold | Made of hard bone | *Made of cartilage, not bone
exercise: Which of these is a cartilaginous fish? | *Skate | Goldfish | Trout | Salmon
exercise: Ben says, «My nose feels cartilaginous.» What is he telling you? | His nose is wet and cold | His nose is covered in fur | *His nose is made of tough, bendy tissue | His nose is made of hard bone
test: «A ray has a cartilaginous skeleton, so it is flexible.» What does the word cartilaginous tell you about the skeleton? | Made of water | *Made of cartilage, which is tough and bendy | Made of bone | Made of metal
test: «The goldfish has a bony skeleton, but the shark is cartilaginous.» What is the difference between them? | *The shark's skeleton is cartilage, the goldfish's is bone | Both have skeletons made of bone | Both have skeletons made of cartilage | The shark is bony and the goldfish is cartilaginous
exam: «Sharks, rays and skates are cartilaginous fish, while salmon and goldfish are bony fish.» Which group does a skate belong to? | Shellfish | *Cartilaginous fish | Bony fish | Mammals
